```rust
fn backticked_tokens(md: &str) -> Vec<(String, usize)> {
    let mut out = Vec::new();
    for (i, line) in md.lines().enumerate() {
        let mut parts = line.split('`');
        parts.next(); // text before the first tick
        let mut toggle = true;
        for part in parts {
            if toggle { out.push((part.to_string(), i+1)); }
            toggle = !toggle;
        }
    }
    out
}
```
This treats each line independently and pairs ticks within a line. A tick left unpaired on a line means subsequent "pairs" shift on that line only — acceptable (limit noted). Careful with CLAUDE.md lines containing a single backtick (unclosed) — that would shift pairing within that line. Let me check CLAUDE.md for lines with odd tick counts. Let me measure.

