```rust
/// Rust-shaped: a snake_case token of at least 4 chars, or a CamelCase token of
/// at least 3.
fn is_rust_symbol_shaped(tok: &str) -> bool { is_fn_shaped(tok) || is_type_shaped(tok) }

fn is_fn_shaped(t: &str) -> bool {
    let b = t.as_bytes();
    if b.len() < 4 { return false; }
    if !(b[0].is_ascii_lowercase() || b[0] == b'_') { return false; }
    b[1..].iter().all(|c| c.is_ascii_lowercase() || c.is_ascii_digit() || *c == b'_')
}

fn is_type_shaped(t: &str) -> bool {
    let b = t.as_bytes();
    if b.len() < 3 { return false; }
    if !b[0].is_ascii_uppercase() { return false; }
    b[1..].iter().all(|c| c.is_ascii_alphanumeric() || *c == b'_')
}
```
Note: planner's regexes `[a-z_][a-z0-9_]{3,}` and `[A-Z][A-Za-z0-9_]{2,}` — exactly these. Confirmed fn occurrences 96 / type 38 / unique 81 matches planner.

Careful: `is_ascii_lowercase` for b[0] plus `_`. And for the rest, `_` allowed. Matches regex.

