`identifier_occurs`:
```rust
fn is_ident_byte(b: u8) -> bool { b.is_ascii_alphanumeric() || b == b'_' }

fn identifier_occurs(haystack: &str, needle: &str) -> bool {
    if needle.is_empty() { return false; }
    for (idx, _) in haystack.match_indices(needle) {
        let bytes = haystack.as_bytes();
        let before = idx == 0 || !is_ident_byte(bytes[idx - 1]);
        let end = idx + needle.len();
        let after = end >= bytes.len() || !is_ident_byte(bytes[end]);
        if before && after { return true; }
    }
    false
}
```
Careful: `end >= bytes.len()` — end can't exceed. Fine.

Note: `bytes[idx-1]` where idx>0 is fine; if the preceding char is multibyte, its last byte is >= 0x80 → not ident byte → before = true. Correct semantics ("the char before is not an identifier char"). Good.

classify:

```rust
fn classify(mentions: &[Mention], src_files: &[(String, String)], register: &[(&str, &str, &str)]) -> Vec<DocSymbolViolation> {
    if src_files.is_empty() { return vec![DocSymbolViolation::EmptySourceScan]; }
    if mentions.is_empty() { return vec![DocSymbolViolation::EmptyCandidateScan]; }
    let src = src_files.iter().map(|(_, t)| t.as_str()).collect::<Vec<_>>().join("\n");

    let mut violations = Vec::new();
    for m in mentions {
        let live = identifier_occurs(&src, &m.symbol);
        let entry = register.iter().find(|(n, _, _)| *n == m.symbol.as_str());
        match (live, entry) {
            (false, None) => violations.push(Unregistered { symbol, line }),
            (true, Some((_, category, _))) => violations.push(RegisteredButLive { symbol, category }),
            _ => {}
        }
    }
    for (name, category, reason) in register {
        if !KNOWN_CATEGORIES.contains(category) { UnknownCategory }
        if reason.trim().is_empty() { EmptyReason }
        if !mentions.iter().any(|m| m.symbol == *name) { RegisteredSymbolVanished }
    }
    violations
}
```
Careful: `mentions` contains duplicates (one per mention site). If the same registered symbol is mentioned twice, the loop pushes... `(false, None)` → Unregistered twice (once per mention). For unregistered: report per mention (with its line) — could duplicate for a repeated unregistered symbol. Fine, informative. Actually let me dedupe by iterating over unique symbols but keeping the first mention line. Hmm, `(true, Some(..))` — a symbol mentioned twice and live would produce two RegisteredButLive violations. Dedupe is cleaner. I'll iterate `unique_symbols` with first-mention line.

Let me restructure: build `Vec<(String, usize)>` = unique (symbol, first line).

```rust
fn unique_mentions(mentions: &[Mention]) -> Vec<Mention> {
    let mut out: Vec<Mention> = Vec::new();
    for m in mentions {
        if !out.iter().any(|o| o.symbol == m.symbol) { out.push(m.clone()); }
    }
    out
}
```
Then classify uses `unique_mentions(mentions)` internally. Cleaner for tests too.

